Predicted defect, not yet run. rootAnchorAdmission.current() needs directAnchorRole, which is writable or Follower only (cmd/kudurru/serving_anchor_activation.go:31-44). With anchorMode managed, a node that becomes Fenced or Conflict therefore:
- fails managed preparation (serving_anchor_bundle.go:176-179), so the DNS-only bundle from D360 is never built;
- fails inputCurrent() (serving_anchor_bundle.go:97-102), so captureRootAnchorOutput refuses every answer, authoritative included (serving_anchor_output.go:36-48);
- cannot restart, because admitAnchors returns errAnchorPolicy (serving_anchor_activation.go:56-59) and admitAnchorEdges refuses a DNS-only token (:86).
The D360 regression (serving_anchor_dnsonly_test.go:15) uses a static fixture.

Fix: split serving admission from updater/poller admission. Serving admission should accept Fenced and Conflict for the same member, publish through the existing DNSOnly token path (serving_anchor_bundle.go:204) with the last accepted managed owner and local denial, and start no updater. Decide and record whether the deny-only supervisor keeps polling on Fenced/Conflict (serving_anchor_follower_supervisor.go:122 and serving_anchor_follower.go:45,109 require Follower); recommended yes. Check that the managed registration apply in internal/store/sqlite/anchor_publication.go accepts PublicationOptions{DNSOnly:true}.

The only 'pre-change codec' proof (old be4446fc decoder keeps format-1 bytes and rejects format 2) lives in gitignored .context/anchor-recovery-20261108/ (compatibility_export_test.go, old-codec/, format1.json, format2.json); nothing in tree pins the bytes. Add:
- committed golden documents for pure format 1 and format 2, an accepted root plus chunk rows (accepted.FormatVersion 1) and a managed local-carrier record;
- tests that Decode then Encode is byte-identical and the version digests are stable;
- unknown pure format 3 and unknown accepted or local format refused, with the store image unchanged on install;
- a tripwire pinning the tuple (store.SchemaVersion=9, replication.FeatureNames(), trustanchors.FormatVersion=1, RecoveryFormatVersion=2, accepted.FormatVersion=1), so a future format change must come with a schema or feature bump.

After the above, rerun on the final commit:
- the storage suite (1,026 entries, 280 s on Nov 8; needs -timeout=10m);
- the composed command suite with the pinned dnsdist test enabled (133 entries, 167 s);
- follower (27 entries, 256 s) and offline recovery (8 entries, 66 s);
- enrolled process scenarios including the new managed variants;
- interop with named and Knot;
- full configured lint and hosted CI.
The pinned dnsdist test is opt-in and never runs in hosted CI (serve_anchor_edge_live_test.go:34-36), so its unskipped local result must be recorded for G23.
